fact WorkItem(id: "WI-732", description: some(value: "WI-714 follow-up: project -- multi-column over a COMPUTED receiver, and the Project[T, keep] type constructor (retire the stamp + idempotency handler). CONTEXT: proposal 052 project increment (07e15fdb). r.(f1, f2) selects relation columns. project has NO lambda, so unlike where/join there is no compile-time macro: the typer synthesizes project_run(r, <spec>) DIRECTLY off the dot form and STAMPS the projected schema (a 4th DotApply dispatch mode for the single-column case; a check_tuple_literal_constructor pre-check for multi-column, recognizing a name-keyed tuple whose fields are ALL DotApply(rel, col) on the SAME leaf receiver via projection_receivers_same = Rc-ptr-eq else leaf-sym). TWO DEFERRED ITEMS: (1) MULTI-COLUMN over a COMPUTED (non-leaf) receiver -- projection_receivers_same identifies the shared receiver by Rc-ptr-eq else leaf symbol, which covers a let-bound computed receiver ('let f = r.where(..); f.(a,b)' WORKS, verified) but not every non-leaf shape; the inline chain 'r.where(..).(a,b)' is a LOUD error (the WI-443 chain limit), not a silent tuple-of-relations. (2) The DESIGN note (NOT a bug): a Project[T, keep] TYPE CONSTRUCTOR -- mirroring join's Concat and fix's Without -- would make project_run's signature SELF-CORRECTING (it currently declares the nominal -> Relation[T = r.T] and relies on the typer's stamp, plus a defensive relation_projection_type idempotency handler in check_apply_iter that is verified NOT currently reached). With Project[T, keep] the schema would reduce at the same return-type normalization boundary Concat/Without reduce at, retiring both the stamp and the idempotency handler and putting all three algebra schema ops on ONE mechanism. The current shape is legitimized by the field_access INC-1b stamp+re-derive precedent, and encoding a keep-spec in TYPE position is awkward -- hence deferred, not wrong. ALSO: duplicate result keys are pre-existing + surface-guarded at parse (convert.rs:1164 validate_projection_labels). ACCEPTANCE: multi-column projection over the deferred computed-receiver shapes either works or is a loud error naming the fix; if Project[T, keep] is taken, project_run's signature is self-correcting and the stamp + relation_projection_type handler are GONE, with Concat/Without/Project sharing one reduction boundary; nothing keyed on project's identity in the typer; existing wi714_project tests green; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-714"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-18T17:28:39Z"))
